       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin (about 2,000 mg per day for extended-release). A dose this high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nCould you tell me which of these you meant?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg per day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total per day.** This could be 850 mg twice daily, or 500 mg three times daily if you want a lower dose.\n- **Something else.** If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd suggest adding a note with the rationale.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
